# 4. FINAL ARENA EXIT GATE — ACTUAL OPENING ANIMATION

The existing ending sequence needs improvement.

When the player completes the campaign and reaches the final arena exit gate, the gate must actually open through a visible animation.

Do not simply teleport the player outside or instantly change the gate state.

### 4.1 Gate Opening Sequence

After the final boss is defeated and the spectator zombies have collapsed:

1. The player automatically walks toward the large exit gate.
2. The player approaches the designated stopping point.
3. The camera focuses briefly on the gate.
4. A mechanical sound begins.
5. The gate starts unlocking.
6. Chains and mechanical components move.
7. The gate slowly opens.
8. Dust falls from the surrounding structure.
9. Metal creaking and heavy mechanical sounds play.
10. Light from the outside environment becomes visible.
11. The gate reaches its fully open position.
12. The player automatically continues walking through the entrance.

### 4.2 Physical Animation

The gate must have real movement.

Depending on the existing model:
- Metal doors rotate around hinges.
- Sliding doors move along tracks.
- Mechanical supports move appropriately.
- Chains and handles animate.
- Gate components remain physically aligned.

Avoid moving the entire gate model without animating its individual mechanical behavior when the model supports it.

### 4.3 Cinematic Presentation

Use:
- Slow camera movement.
- Heavy mechanical sound.
- Subtle camera shake.
- Falling dust.
- Environmental lighting changes.
- Exterior visibility reveal.

Do not immediately fade to black when the gate begins opening.

The player must be able to see the gate opening.

The automatic movement system must wait until the gate has reached a safe and fully open position.

Then resume player movement.

